Subject: [PATCH 26/62] verimark: sanitize source comments for upstream
 submission
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Comment-only cleanup ahead of the upstream MR : remove internal
development markers (Phase 5-10.3.x), references to private docs
paths and tooling (python PoC, tools/, docs/), low-level RE notes
(Ghidra symbols, WindDbg, etc.), and the "Realtek/ipw2200 pattern"
analogy.

Kept :
- Tudor protocol naming (Synaptics family name, neutral)
- Synaptics quirk documentation (useful for maintainers — just no
  longer says HOW we observed it)
- RFC references (RFC 5246 §7.4.9 etc.)
- Wire-format and opcode specifications
- Module-level architecture explanations

No code or behavior changes. 11 standalone TDD suites stay green ;
libfprint builds clean against libgusb 0.4.9 on NixOS.

AI-assisted.
